     A                                  1 34'COLLATE MENU'
     A                                  3  1'You may use this routine to specif-
     A                                      y the sequence in which your depart-
     A                                      ments'
     A                                  4  1'are presented or the sequence in w-
     A                                      hich your classifications within a'
     A                                  4 70'depart-'
     A                                  5  1'ment are presented.  WARNING both'
     A                                  5 35'of these routines may use a lot of'
     A                                  5 70'computer'
     A                                  6  1'time depending on how many records'
     A                                  6 36'it has to modify.  Please use thes-
     A                                      e routines'
     A                                  7  1'during low activity periods.  Note'
     A                                  7 36'also that they may keep your keybo-
     A                                      ard locked'
     A                                  8  1'up for 5 to 10 minutes so be patie-
     A                                      nt.'
     A                                 10  1'If you specify a collating value f-
     A                                      or one department, you should assig-
     A                                      n a UNIQUE'
     A                                 11  1'collating value for each departmen-
     A                                      t.  Likewise, if you specify a coll-
     A                                      ating valu'
     A                                 12  1'for one classification within a de-
     A                                      partment you should assign a UNIQUE-
     A                                       value for'
     A                                 13  1'each classification within that de-
     A                                      partment.'
     A                                 14  6'Departments assigned identical col-
     A                                      lating values in the hundrends and'
     A                                 14 75'tens'
     A                                 15  1'columns will be printed together o-
     A                                      n the attendance report.  If either-
     A                                       the'
     A                                 16  1'hundrends or tens column is differ-
     A                                      ent, they will be printed seperatel-
     A                                      y.  (ie.'
     A                                 17  1'101 and 100 will be printed togeth-
     A                                      er but 201 and 211 will be printed'
     A                                 17 70'seperately)'
     A                                 19  1'Press f5 to collate departments or'
     A                                 19 36'enter a department number and pres-
     A                                      s f6'
     A                                 20  1'to collate classifications within'
     A                                 20 35'a department.'
     A                                 22 31'Dept.'
     A            DEPT           4Y 0B 22 37DSPATR(UL)
     A                                      CHECK(RB)
     A                                      OVRDTA
     A                                      OVRATR
     A  01                                  DSPATR(RI)
     A  01
     AO 97 96                               DSPATR(PC)
